## 3. Problems Encountered & Fixed

| # | Problem | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Wrong virtual environment active (`.venv` instead of `venv`) caused file-not-found errors | Deactivated and reactivated the correct `venv` |
| 2 | File saved with a typo (`lint_db.py` instead of `init_db.py`) | Renamed using `Rename-Item` |
| 3 | File saved with incorrect capitalization (`Models.py` instead of `models.py`) — would have broken the `from app import models` import | Renamed to lowercase to match the import statement exactly |
| 4 | `init_db.py` initially placed inside `app/` instead of the outer `backend/` folder | Moved one level up using `Move-Item` |

> Reinforces a pattern from Day 4: exact file names, capitalization, and folder placement matter in Python imports — these are quick fixes once spotted, and good practice for catching them early.

